  "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-3t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121715/assets/362ee182f39f9d5cc1e7597f7e836a6ce802b4762a03c347c5701c0830f3d523.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{-3t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{-5t})^{′}}=\\frac{-3{c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}}{-5{c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}}=\\frac{3{c}_{2}}{5{c}_{1}}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to \\pm \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more vertical as the trajectories approach the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121715/assets/bff6e7e5f4772441cdc81c809eadc377d3c2c43bd653d0c5c4f7f306adf79a5e.png)",
